<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">New Caledonia (Darien)</h1><p class="st-meta">1698 CE – 1700 CE · capital New Edinburgh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Scotland's disastrous attempt to found a trading colony on the Isthmus of Panama, whose failure helped push Scotland into union with England in 1707.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Company of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, promoted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-paterson-banker">William Paterson</a> and backed by perhaps a fifth of Scotland's liquid capital, aimed to build an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepôt</a> linking the Atlantic and Pacific. About 1,200 colonists sailed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leith">Leith</a> in July 1698 and landed at Darien in November, founding Fort St Andrew and the town of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony was run by a council of quarrelling members, with no clear leader. Settlers found the soil poor, the trade goods unsuited to local markets and the climate deadly; fever killed hundreds. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-england">William III</a>, wary of offending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, forbade English colonies to supply them. Relations with the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guna-people">Guna people</a> were friendly, but Spain regarded the colony as an intrusion.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The first settlers abandoned Darien in June 1699. A second expedition arrived later that year, won a skirmish at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-toubacanti">Toubacanti</a>, but capitulated to a Spanish siege at the end of March 1700 and left in April. The loss of capital weakened Scottish resistance to union, and the 1707 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acts-of-union-1707">Act of Union</a> included compensation for the company's investors.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/new-caledonia-darien.jpg" alt="New Caledonia (Darien)" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Company_of_Scotland_Trading_to_Africa_and_the_Indies.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1698 CE – 1700 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New Edinburgh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William Paterson</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Presbyterianism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Scots and English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/panama">Panama</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Darien scheme, Caledonia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1699&amp;focus=new-caledonia-darien" aria-label="New Caledonia (Darien) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2536 1848 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where New Caledonia (Darien) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2856 2104L4892 500"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4892 500h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2856 2104h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2856 2104h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1699&amp;focus=new-caledonia-darien">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

